# Protected-path ownership metadata for adopters who choose to enable review.
#
# The template's main ruleset does not require approving reviews. Replace
# @shunmd before enabling code-owner review in a generated project.
#
# A code owner must have write access to the repository the file lives in.
# Replace every @shunmd below with your own account or team before turning that
# rule on. See the customization checklist in README.md.
#
# The protected-file-notice workflow still reports changes to these paths, but
# the notice is informational and does not create an approval boundary.
#
# Ordinary application code (`src/`) and documentation are deliberately NOT
# listed. The point of this repository's quality gate is that changes there are
# judged by the checks, not by a human reading a diff. Listing everything here
# would put human review back in front of exactly the work it is meant to
# replace.
#
# Last match wins, so the specific paths follow the general ones.

# The enforcement layer: the configuration that decides whether anything else
# passes. If these could be edited without review, every other gate would be
# advisory.
/package.json                   @shunmd
/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @shunmd
/pnpm-workspace.yaml            @shunmd
/mise.toml                      @shunmd
/mise.lock                      @shunmd
/tsconfig.json                  @shunmd
/eslint.config.js               @shunmd
/prettier.config.js             @shunmd
/.prettierignore                @shunmd
/vitest.config.ts               @shunmd
/stryker.config.json            @shunmd
/knip.jsonc                     @shunmd
/.dependency-cruiser.json       @shunmd
/.jscpd.json                    @shunmd
/.editorconfig                  @shunmd
/.gitattributes                 @shunmd

# CI, repository settings, and the scripts that enforce policy.
/.github/                       @shunmd
/infra/                         @shunmd
/scripts/                       @shunmd

# Accepted exceptions to the dependency policy. Every entry here is a decision
# to ship with a known advisory or a non-default licence, which is precisely
# the kind of judgement a machine must not make alone.
/infra/policy/                  @shunmd

# The always-loaded agent instructions. A change here changes how every future
# agent behaves in this repository.
/AGENTS.md                      @shunmd
/CLAUDE.md                      @shunmd

# Agent skills. Loaded on demand rather than at startup, so they do not change
# every task the way the files above do -- but they tell an agent how to edit
# the enforcement layer, which is the same authority at one remove.
/.claude/                       @shunmd
